# Employee onboarding, step by step, for the HTTP client of IntelliJ IDEA.
#
# Start the engine on port 8080 and zenbpm-ui as examples/README.md says, then either twin of this
# example (README "Run it"); both answer on port 8105. Run the requests of a scenario one after the
# other. A step which reads the onboarding checks where it stands: a red check means "not yet", run
# it again. zenbpm-ui shows each onboarding as an instance of
# employee-onboarding__employee_onboarding whose business key is the onboarding's id, and the
# workplace it calls as an instance of employee-onboarding__workplace_provisioning beneath it.

@app = http://localhost:8105

### EmployeeOnboardingIT#aNewEmployeeIsOnboardedOnceTheWelcomeMeetingIsHeld: 1. the contract is signed
POST {{app}}/onboardings
Content-Type: application/json

{"employeeName": "Jane Doe", "position": "backend developer", "startDate": "2026-11-02"}

> {%
    client.global.set("onboarding", response.body.onboardingId);
%}

### 2. accounts created, laptop and badge ready (EmployeeOnboardingIT#theCalledProcessPreparesTheWorkplaceWithBothBranchesKept)
GET {{app}}/onboardings/{{onboarding}}

> {%
    client.test("the welcome meeting is due, with the whole workplace", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "WELCOME_MEETING_DUE", "status is " + response.body.status);
        client.assert(response.body.emailAddress !== null, "no accounts yet");
        client.assert(response.body.laptopSerialNumber !== null, "no laptop");
        client.assert(response.body.badgeNumber !== null, "no badge");
    });
%}

### 3. HR holds the welcome meeting
POST {{app}}/onboardings/{{onboarding}}/welcome-meeting
Content-Type: application/json

{"notes": "met the team, got the keys"}

### 4. onboarded: the end of the workflow reached the application (it logs "welcome aboard")
GET {{app}}/onboardings/{{onboarding}}

> {%
    client.test("onboarded", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "ONBOARDED", "status is " + response.body.status);
        client.assert(response.body.welcomeMeetingNotes === "met the team, got the keys", "notes are " + response.body.welcomeMeetingNotes);
    });
%}

### EmployeeOnboardingIT#aWelcomeMeetingWhichIsNotDueIsRefused: the welcome meeting of the onboarding above, a second time
POST {{app}}/onboardings/{{onboarding}}/welcome-meeting
Content-Type: application/json

{"notes": "once more"}

> {%
    client.test("409 Conflict", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### EmployeeOnboardingIT#aWelcomeMeetingWhichIsNotDueIsRefused: the welcome meeting of an onboarding nobody started
POST {{app}}/onboardings/no-such-onboarding/welcome-meeting
Content-Type: application/json

{"notes": "who is this?"}

> {%
    client.test("404 Not Found", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### EmployeeOnboardingIT#anIncompleteNewHireIsRefused: a new hire without a start date
POST {{app}}/onboardings
Content-Type: application/json

{"employeeName": "Jane Doe", "position": "backend developer"}

> {%
    client.test("400 Bad Request", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

# Not here: EmployeeOnboardingIT#aWelcomeMeetingReportedSeveralTimesAtOnceIsAcceptedOnce sends eight
# reports at the same moment, which an HTTP client that sends one request after the other cannot do.
